Port Embree 4.4.1 to powerpc64le.

Embree's kernels are written against SSE intrinsics and selected by the
__SSE*__ macros.  GCC (>= 8) and clang ship <xmmintrin.h> .. <nmmintrin.h>
for powerpc64le that implement SSE through SSE4.2 on VSX (POWER8+), gated
behind -DNO_WARN_X86_INTRINSICS.  This is the same shape as Embree's own
AArch64 port (sse2neon), with a far smaller shim:

- CMakeLists.txt / common/cmake/{gnu,clang}.cmake: detect ppc64le
  (EMBREE_PPC64LE), give the SSE2/SSE4.2 ISA flag sets the -D__SSE*__
  defines plus -DNO_WARN_X86_INTRINSICS -mvsx, make the AVX probes fail so
  AVX+ stay off, add -fsigned-char/-flax-vector-conversions as on ARM
  (char is unsigned on POWER too), and map the ISPC target to vsx-i32x4.
- common/simd/ppc/emulation.h (new): the intrinsics the compat headers lack:
  _mm_getcsr/_mm_setcsr and the MXCSR FTZ/DAZ/exception-mask macros (no-ops,
  POWER has no MXCSR and no denormal penalty), _mm_dp_ps, _mm_insert_ps,
  _mm_popcnt_u32/u64, _mm_stream_load_si128.
- common/sys/platform.h: __64BIT__ on __powerpc64__.
- common/sys/intrinsics.h, thread.cpp: include the shim instead of
  <immintrin.h>/<xmmintrin.h>.
- common/sys/sysinfo.cpp: report vendor "IBM" and a fixed SSE..SSE4.2+POPCNT
  feature set (every POWER8+ has VSX; there is nothing to dispatch on).

Verified on POWER9: builds with GCC 16, rtcIntersect1/rtcIntersect4 return
correct hits/misses, embree selects sse42::BVH4Triangle4Intersector4Hybrid.

Portability fix, worth sending upstream (github.com/RenderKit/embree).
Local choice, not part of the patch: the PKGBUILD builds only the SSE4.2
ISA (EMBREE_ISA_SSE2=OFF) since POWER8+ always has it.

